<title>HONG KONG: Dransfield year net loss HK$21.4 mln.</title>
<headline>Dransfield year net loss HK$21.4 mln.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-08-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended March 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   5.54 loss  vs 5.85 gain</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    nil	  vs 1.0</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  11.66 loss vs nil</p>
<p>    Net			    21.40 loss vs 21.60 profit</p>
<p>    Turnover		     764.41     vs 656.40</p>
<p>    Company name		 Dransfield Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  September 24-30</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   N/A</p>
<p>NOTE - Dransfield is a marketer of consumer electronics goods and appliances, food and beverages.</p>
<p>The group's investment in a joint venture, which was previously accounted for as a subsidiary, has been reclassified as an associated company in the current year presentation as all significant decisions have to be agreed unilaterally by all investing parties.</p>
<p>Net is after an exceptional loss mainly on provision for doubtful debts.</p>
<p>Total dividend for year is one H.K. cent (including interim dividend of one cent) vs two cents.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
